*** Settings ***
Documentation     Creating Sequence Definitions (BR §4.1-§4.3, AC05-AC08, AC23, AC44). The first
...               test saves the definition under test, consumed by the later suites.
Resource          resources/sequence.resource
Suite Setup       Run Keywords    Create Authorized API Session    AND    Ensure Sequence Org
Test Tags         essential    sequence_definition    create


*** Test Cases ***
Create With Required Fields Succeeds
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    prefix_template=RB    padding=${3}    initial_value=${0}
    ...    increment=${2}
    ${id}    ${etag}=    Response Should Be Create Success    ${resp}
    Set Global Variable    ${SEQ_DEFINITION_ID}    ${id}
    Set Global Variable    ${SEQ_DEFINITION_ETAG}    ${etag}

Create Keeps An Explicit Zero Initial Value
    [Documentation]    AC05 starts at 0. The server defaults initial_value to 1 only when it is
    ...    absent; an explicit 0 must survive.
    ${item}=    Read Sequence Definition    ${SEQ_DEFINITION_ID}
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[initial_value]    0
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[increment]    2
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[padding]    3
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[prefix_template]    RB

Create Fills The Server Defaults
    [Documentation]    BR §4.2: padding 5, initial 1, increment 1, never resets, Sequence-formatted,
    ...    increment algorithm, 90 days of issuance retention; scope_type derived from the scope.
    ${id}    ${etag}=    Create Sequence Definition
    ${item}=    Read Sequence Definition    ${id}
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[padding]    5
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[initial_value]    1
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[increment]    1
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[reset_period]    never
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[format_owner]    sequence
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[algorithm]    increment
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[issuance_retention_days]    90
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[scope_type]    org
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[org_id]    ${SEQ_ORG_ID}
    Should Not Be Empty    ${item}[timezone]
    Dictionary Should Not Contain Key    ${item}    first_issued_at
    [Teardown]    Archive Sequence Definition    ${id}

Create Lowercases The Sub Scope Into The Scope Type
    [Documentation]    SEQ-DEF-01: sub_scope is stored lowercase and scope_type is computed as
    ...    <configuration_scope>.<sub_scope>.
    ${id}    ${etag}=    Create Sequence Definition    sub_scope=Robot_Shelf
    ${item}=    Read Sequence Definition    ${id}
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[sub_scope]    robot_shelf
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[scope_type]    org.robot_shelf
    [Teardown]    Archive Sequence Definition    ${id}

Create Pseudorandom Forces Padding To Zero
    [Documentation]    SEQ-004: an FF1 code has its own width, so padding is always 0, whatever the
    ...    client sent. The API names the algorithm "pseudorandom"; the generated key stays inside.
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    algorithm=pseudorandom    padding=${4}    prefix_template=CORE
    ${id}    ${etag}=    Response Should Be Create Success    ${resp}
    ${resp}=    GET On Session    api    ${SEQ_DEFINITION_API}/${id}
    ${item}=    Item Should Match Schema    ${resp}    ${SEQ_SCHEMA_DIR}/sequence_definition.json    200
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[algorithm]    pseudorandom
    Should Be Equal As Integers    ${item}[padding]    0
    Response Should Carry No Secret    ${resp}
    [Teardown]    Archive Sequence Definition    ${id}

Create With The Stored Algorithm Spelling Fails
    [Documentation]    FF1_FPE is the storage name only; the API vocabulary is "pseudorandom".
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    algorithm=FF1_FPE
    Response Status Should Be    ${resp}    400
    Should Be Equal    ${resp.json()}[0][field]    algorithm

Create With Algorithm Params Fails
    [Documentation]    algorithm_params is generated by the server and never crosses the API.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    algorithm=pseudorandom    algorithm_params=${{ {'key': '00'} }}
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_READ_ONLY_FIELD}    algorithm_params

Create With A Server Owned Field Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    scope_type=org.forged
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_READ_ONLY_FIELD}    scope_type
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    first_issued_at=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_READ_ONLY_FIELD}    first_issued_at

Create With A Zero Increment Fails
    [Documentation]    AC07. A zero step would issue the same number forever.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    increment=${0}
    Response Should Be Invalid Number Range Error    ${resp}    increment

Create With A Negative Increment Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    increment=${-1}
    Response Should Be Invalid Number Range Error    ${resp}    increment

Create With A Zero Padding Fails
    [Documentation]    AC07: padding is 1-32 for the increment algorithm.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    padding=${0}
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_PADDING}    padding

Create With A Padding Above 32 Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    padding=${33}
    Response Should Be Invalid Number Range Error    ${resp}    padding

Create With A Negative Initial Value Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    initial_value=${-1}
    Response Should Be Invalid Number Range Error    ${resp}    initial_value

Create With An Unknown Time Zone Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    timezone=Mars/Olympus_Mons
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_INVALID_TIMEZONE}    timezone

Create With An Unknown Template Variable Fails
    [Documentation]    AC08.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    prefix_template=%(warehouse)s/
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_INVALID_TEMPLATE}    prefix_template

Create With A Broken Template Escape Fails
    [Documentation]    AC08: an unterminated placeholder is neither a variable nor literal text.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    prefix_template=INV-%(year
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_INVALID_TEMPLATE}    prefix_template

Create With A Prefix Ending In A Digit Fails
    [Documentation]    AC44 / SEQ-UNIQ-02: "A1" + "23" and "A12" + "3" would render the same code.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    prefix_template=A1
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_INVALID_TEMPLATE}    prefix_template

Create With A Suffix Starting With A Digit Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    suffix_template=7X
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_INVALID_TEMPLATE}    suffix_template

Create A Resetting Definition Without A Period Marker Fails
    [Documentation]    AC23 / SEQ-TIME-05: a yearly reset restarts at the initial value, so the code
    ...    must carry the year or two years would issue the same code.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    reset_period=yearly    prefix_template=INV-
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_INVALID_TEMPLATE}    prefix_template

Create A Resetting Definition With A Period Marker Succeeds
    ${id}    ${etag}=    Create Sequence Definition    reset_period=yearly    prefix_template=INV-%(range_year)s-
    ${item}=    Read Sequence Definition    ${id}
    Should Be Equal    ${item}[reset_period]    yearly
    [Teardown]    Archive Sequence Definition    ${id}

Create A Tenant Definition With An Org Fails
    [Documentation]    AC03: a tenant-wide definition belongs to no organization.
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    configuration_scope=tenant
    Response Should Be Sequence Error    ${resp}    ${SEQ_ERR_INVALID_INPUT}    org_id

Create An Org Definition Without An Org Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    org_id=${None}
    Response Should Be Missing Fields Error    ${resp}    org_id

Create With An Invalid Code Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    code=Robot Code
    Response Status Should Be    ${resp}    400
    Should Be Equal    ${resp.json()}[0][field]    code

Create With A Duplicate Code In The Org Fails
    [Documentation]    AC01/AC02: one definition per (code, org).
    [Tags]    negative
    ${item}=    Read Sequence Definition    ${SEQ_DEFINITION_ID}
    ${resp}=    Post Sequence Definition    code=${item}[code]
    Response Status Should Be    ${resp}    400
    Should Be Equal    ${resp.json()}[0][key]    common:err_unique_constraint_violated

Create With Missing Required Fields Fails
    [Tags]    negative
    ${resp}=    POST On Session    api    ${SEQ_DEFINITION_API}    json=${{ {} }}    expected_status=any
    Response Should Be Missing Fields Error    ${resp}    configuration_scope    owner_module    code    name

